 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the correction law, in relation to providing information\nregarding medicare part B coverage to certain individuals",
    "basePrintNo": "S3175",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S3175-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §71, Cor L",
    "lawSection": "Correction Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S3175\n\nSPONSOR: CLEARE\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the correction law, in relation to providing information\nregarding medicare part B coverage to certain individuals\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nTo inform individuals of their continued medicare coverage upon incar-\nceration and provide them with information concerning termination of\ntheir coverage for their duration of stay within the correctional facil-\nity.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSection one of the bill adds a new subdivision 7-a to Section 71 of the\ncorrection law requiring the department, upon receiving information of a\nperson's admission to a correctional facility, to provide persons\ncommitted with information regarding termination of medicare part B\ncoverage for the duration of incarceration. ò\n\nSection 2 of the bill in the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nCurrently, when a Medicare part B recipient is incarcerated, their\ncoverage does not automatically discontinue. This can result in the\nindividual having to pay the monthly premium even though they are unable\nto utilize Medicare while in prison or jail. As of 2022, the monthly\npremium is $170.10. This can result in individuals having to pay back\nsubstantial overdue premiums to Medicare.This bill does not require the\nindividual to forego Medicare benefits, it simply requires the depart-\nment to provide information on how they can voluntarily terminate their\ncoverage while incarcerated.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to state.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
